cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MRISim in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MRISim: an interactive MRI physics simulator"
abstract: >-
  A dual-edition (desktop + in-browser) MRI physics simulator that models the
  signal chain from tissue properties and pulse-sequence parameters through
  k-space acquisition to the reconstructed image — covering the major clinical
  contrast mechanisms, acquisition strategies, and artifacts — with a guided
  teaching layer and a Qt-free headless API for scripted research use.
authors:
  - family-names: Akkoc
    given-names: Erol
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ea1188/mrisim"
url: "https://ea1188.github.io/mrisim/"
version: 1.56.0
date-released: 2026-07-01
keywords:
  - MRI
  - magnetic resonance imaging
  - physics simulation
  - pulse sequences
  - k-space
  - medical imaging education
  - Pyodide
